2026-08-05T09:09:05+00:00,DAERA Forestry Grants,https://www.daera-ni.gov.uk/articles/daera-forestry-grants,Northern Ireland,"EU / international, Northern Ireland, Republic of Ireland","agriculture, forestry, biodiversity",35,,,,"10 grant signals; category keywords: agriculture, forestry, biodiversity; NI / border region keywords; closed phrase found","Almost all woodlands in Northern Ireland are planted with some form of grant assistance. The Forest Service encourages the creation of new woodlands and the management of existing woodlands by providing grant aid towards the cost of the work. Forests for Our Future programme aims to plant 18 million trees or 9,000 hectares of new woodland over the next 10 years to help our environment and economy. Grant funding for creating new woodlands will be via the Small Woodland Grant Scheme or the Forest Expansion Scheme.",closed phrase found
